"degas_log2fc":0.111532,"degas_padj":0.000253409},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"CACNA1A","gene_symbol_current":"CACNA1A","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":2.38928e-37,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.326099,"nucleus_score":-13.2123,"pct_ad":0.910379,"pct_control":0.923285,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.991471,"donor_log2fc":-0.301833,"donor_lfcse":0.124844,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.97488e-05,"degas_log2fc":-0.264512,"degas_padj":2.56429e-28},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"CACNA1A","gene_symbol_current":"CACNA1A","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":4.41542e-09,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.102443,"nucleus_score":-6.02591,"pct_ad":0.304659,"pct_control":0.327582,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.984493,"donor_log2fc":-0.020814,"donor_lfcse":0.165089,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00159729,"degas_log2fc":-0.178181,"degas_padj":2.6027e-17}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","module":"blue","kme":0.258703,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.506562,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","module":"yellow","kme":0.373863,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.552322,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","module":"yellow","kme":0.142882,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.398013,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","module":"brown","kme":0.342086,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","module":"brown","kme":0.224476,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000141837","entrez_id":["773"],"uniprot":["O00555"],"ncbi_summary":"Voltage-dependent calcium channels mediate the entry of calcium ions into excitable cells, and are also involved in a variety of calcium-dependent processes, including muscle contraction, hormone or neurotransmitter release, and gene expression. Calcium channels are multisubunit complexes composed of alpha-1, beta, alpha-2/delta, and gamma subunits. The channel activity is directed by the pore-forming alpha-1 subunit, whereas, the others act as auxiliary subunits regulating this activity. The distinctive properties of the calcium channel types are related primarily to the expression of a variety of alpha-1 isoforms, alpha-1A, B, C, D, E, and S. This gene encodes the alpha-1A subunit, which is predominantly expressed in neuronal tissue. Mutations in this gene are associated with 2 neurologic disorders, familial hemiplegic migraine and episodic ataxia 2. This gene also exhibits polymorphic variation due to (CAG)n-repeats. Multiple transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene. In one set of transcript variants, the (CAG)n-repeats occur in the 3' UTR, and are not associated with any disease. But in another set of variants, an insertion extends the coding region to include the (CAG)n-repeats which encode a polyglutamine tract. Expansion of the (CAG)n-repeats from the normal 4-18 to 21-33 in the coding region is associated with spinocerebellar ataxia 6. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2016].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O00555","text":"Voltage-sensitive calcium channels (VSCC) mediate the entry of calcium ions into excitable cells and are also involved in a variety of calcium-dependent processes, including muscle contraction, hormone or neurotransmitter release, gene expression, cell motility, cell division and cell death. The isoform alpha-1A gives rise to P and/or Q-type calcium currents. P/Q-type calcium channels belong to the 'high-voltage activated' (HVA) group and are specifically blocked by the spider omega-agatoxin-IVA (AC P54282) (By similarity). They are however insensitive to dihydropyridines (DHP)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"O00555","pdb_id":"8x90","het_id":"PS1","resolution":2.95,"method":"Electron Microscopy","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Green et al. 2024","Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"1,2-DIDECANOYL-SN-GLYCERO-3-[PHOSPHO-L-SERINE]","ligand_class":"lipid, detergent, buffer or other additive","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"P/Q type calcium channel","first_author":"Li, Z.","n_authors":7,"journal":"Cell Res.","year":2024,"doi":"10.1038/s41422-024-00940-5","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41422-024-00940-5"}],"alphafold_accessions":["O00555"]}